source: ASF Jira Server 8.20.10, POST /rest/api/1.0/render (hack/jira-render-evidence.py), captured 2026-08-23
observed: A backslash before the separator protects nothing: the split leaves the target `b`, Jira resolves nothing and shows an error span, so jiro keeps the bracket text literal and warns.
-- input.jira --
[a\|b|http://x]
-- rendered.html --
<p><span class="error">&#91;a\|b|http://x&#93;</span></p>
-- want.md --
\[a\\|b|http://x\]
-- warnings.json --
[
 {
  "Line": 1,
  "Column": 1,
  "Construct": "link",
  "Reason": "backslash before a Jira link separator leaves a target Jira cannot resolve; complete link remains literal"
 }
]
